From bd48f0c75aa45f585972cc4dea11a71d2016f541 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 16:15:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/15] fix(pipeline): restore Projects/Education sections and
 improve PDF text extraction
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three root-cause fixes for the Harshibar template generating truncated resumes:

1. _resume_doc_from_profile_text: parsed.projects_bullets and
   parsed.education_lines were never added to doc.extra_sections.
   The Harshibar template (and any extra-sections-aware template) looks
   there to render PROJECTS and EDUCATION — they were silently dropped.

2. api_upload_resume: was using page.extract_text() which collapses word
   spacing and loses bullet markers on some PDFs. Now uses _extract_pdf_text()
   which reconstructs lines from bounding-box word positions.

3. profile_parser.parse_profile_text: summary was grabbed as "first two long
   lines" — which picks up skills bullets before the actual Summary section.
   Now prefers content found inside a Summary section header; falls back to
   the old heuristic only when no Summary section exists.

Also synced backend files (app.py, profile_parser.py, renderers, templates)
from main to include the Jinja/structured renderer path.

