From 0acb81f1aed19a4b184ed8941d3156348766ab1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 15 May 2026 16:32:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/15] feat(pipeline): LLM extraction+tailoring via Grok
 before Jinja2 render
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replace the regex profile parser as the primary extraction path with an
LLM call (Grok preferred for throughput, Gemini fallback) that:

- Extracts ALL resume sections (experience, projects, education, skills,
  contact) into structured JSON in one shot — no brittle regex
- Simultaneously tailors bullet points and summary to the target JD:
  stronger action verbs, quantified achievements, natural JD keyword fit
- Returns a ResumeDocModel fed directly into the Jinja2 template renderer

The new pipeline:
  PDF text → Grok (JSON schema) → ResumeDocModel → Jinja2 → LaTeX → PDF

Regex parser (_resume_doc_from_profile_text) kept as fallback when the
LLM call fails or no XAI/Gemini key is configured.

https://claude.ai/code/session_015ED4ARZAgLY1ww81cRfeDs
